{
  "_readme": "CARGO sessions: one physical cargo from loading to sale, in day-steps. 'days' (date + benchmark flat price in $/bbl) is filled from real settlements by scripts/build-physical.py. Port basis is MODELED (linear from start to end with seeded noise) around reported levels; there is no free daily basis history. Events are applied at runtime: types port_congestion (+days queued, demurrage), pipeline_outage (basis collapses at the port, widens at widen_ports or all others), weather_delay (+days at sea), refinery_outage (local bid drops), refinery_restart (local bid recovers), demand_spike / demand_fade (local bid jumps / eases), quality_dispute (off-spec penalty $/bbl on sales there). A port's delivered price = flat + that port's basis.",
  "cards": [
    {
      "id": "cg-floating-storage-2020",
      "type": "cargo",
      "category": "physical",
      "difficulty": 3,
      "title": "Floating storage, April 2020",
      "open": "Day after WTI went negative. 500k bbl afloat",
      "cargo": {
        "name": "WTI Midland",
        "api": 42,
        "sulfur": "0.2% sweet",
